    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIEm">II Em</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†*" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.__"/><pb n="188" ed="#liebermann"/>Eac ic ðancige Gode ⁊ eow eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, ðe me wel fylston, ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†**" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.___"/> þæs friðes, ðe we nu habbað æt ðam þyfðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.2"/>; ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> gelyfe ic to eow, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ge willan fylstan to ðissu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> swa miccle bet, swa us is eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mare ðærf, ðæt hit gehealden sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="188" ed="#liebermann"/>Eac ic ðancie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.23"/> Gode ⁊ eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.24"/> eallum, ðe me fylston, ðæs friðes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.25"/>, ðe we nu habbað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.26"/> æt ðam ðyfðam; ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> gelyfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.27"/> ic to eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.24"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ge willan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.28"/> fylstan to ðyssum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.29"/> swa micle bet, swa us is eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mare ðearf, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hit gehealden sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="189" ed="#liebermann"/>Etiam gratias ago Deo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.16"/> et uobis omnibus, qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.17"/> bene iuuatis me, de pace, quam pro furtis nuper instituimus; et ideo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.18"/> confido<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.19"/>, quod adiuuare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.20"/> uelitis ad eam tanto melius, quanto magis opus est nobis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.21"/>, ut conseruata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.oe.22"/> sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="10" ed="#robertson"/>[Þæncunge ðæm ðe wið ðyfþe fylstaþ.] Eac ic ðancie Gode ⁊ eow eallum, ðe me fylston<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIEm_5.robnote.fn.5"/>, ðæs friðes ðe we nu habbað æt ðam ðyfðam<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIEm_5.robnote.fn.6"/>; ðonne gelyfe ic to eow, þæt ge willan fylstan to ðyssum swa micle bet, swa us is eallum mare ðearf ðæt hit gehealden sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="189" ed="#liebermann"/>(Dank<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.de.1"/> denen, welche gegen Diebstahl helfen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>). Ferner dank ich Gott und euch allen, die ihr mir gut geholfen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.de.2"/> habt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.de.3"/>, für die Sicherheit vor Diebstählen, die wir bereits (festgesetzt <hi rend="italic">lq</hi>) haben; ich vertraue nun auf euch, dass ihr zur vorliegenden [Rechtsordnung] um so viel besser helfen wollet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIEm_5.lnote.de.4"/>, als uns allen nöthiger ist, dass dies beobachtet werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Thanks to those who help against theft. Ld) Further I thank God and all of you who have helped me well for the security from thefts that we now have (have established, lq); I trust in you, then, that you will help with the present [legal order] all the better, the more needful it is for all of us that it be observed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIEm_5.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="11" ed="#robertson"/>Further, I thank God and all of you, who have given me full support, for the immunity from thefts which we now enjoy. I therefore confidently expect of you, that you will be all the more willing to give your support towards this [maintenance of the public peace]<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_5.robnote.n.2"/>, in proportion as its observance is a more urgent matter for us all.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="430" ed="#whitelock"/>Further, I thank God and all of you who have well supported me, for the immunity from thefts which we now have; I now trust to you, that you will support this measure so much the better as the need is greater for all of us that it shall be observed.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">H's ‘⁊’ before ‘þæs friðes’ should be struck (so B and Quadr.).</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ce <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ce Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-we <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-we Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fryþes <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fryþes Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hæb. æt ðæm ðyfþe <hi rend="spaced">gesette</hi> <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hæb. æt ðæm ðyfþe <hi rend="italic">gesette</hi> Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gelife <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gelife Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðis. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðis. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">meo <hi rend="italic">fügt R zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">meo added by R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quia <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quia Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in Deo <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in Deo RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">considero <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">considero Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">me <hi rend="spaced">de pace ista</hi> adi. u. tanto <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">me <hi rend="italic">de pace ista</hi> adi. u. tanto MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> uobis <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> uobis <hi rend="italic">THk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from uobis R; uobis THk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">conserta <hi rend="italic">MHk;</hi> consecuta <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">conserta MHk; consecuta Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.__" n="†*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Þæncunge ðæm ðe wiþ ðyfþe fylstaþ <hi rend="italic">Rubrik Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Þæncunge ðæm ðe wiþ ðyfþe fylstaþ rubric Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.___" n="†**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">streiche laut B Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">delete, following B Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">127</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Rieger und Toller s. v. <hi rend="italic">þancung</hi> ergänzen davor <hi rend="italic">Be</hi> ‘Von Dank’, wogegen Q's <hi rend="italic">gratias</hi> spricht. Vielmehr kann Rubrikator Accus. meinen oder <hi rend="italic">-e</hi> ein unorganisches Anhängsel durch Ld, wie an vielen Stellen sein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Rieger and Toller s. v. <hi rend="italic">þancung</hi> supply <hi rend="italic">Be</hi> ‘Of thanks’ before it, which Q’s <hi rend="italic">gratias</hi> argues against. Rather, the rubricator may intend an acc., or the <hi rend="italic">-e</hi> may be an inorganic appendage added by Ld, as in many places</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">127</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘helfet’ Q, was grammatisch möglich. Aber der Ggs. zum nächsten Satze fordert Praeteritum</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘you help’ Q, which is grammatically possible. But the contrast with the next sentence requires the preterite</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">127</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">and</hi> ist H's Fehler gegen B und lq, die den Archetyptext darstellen. Mit Unrecht behalten es Thorpe und Schmid bei. Nicht für ‘Hilfe <hi rend="spaced">und</hi> Polizei’, sondern ‘zur P.’ dankt ‘euch’, d. i. den Witan, auch IV Eg 16.—Die Lesung in lq scheint mir Interpolation, als ‘haben’, mehr auxiliar geworden, seltener ‘besitzen’ bedeutete. Dieselbe Bed. ‘Frieden (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1e) geniessen’ auch II Atr 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">and</hi> is H’s error as against B and lq, which represent the archetype text. Thorpe and Schmid wrongly retain it. IV Eg 16 too thanks ‘you’, i.e. the Witan, not for ‘help <hi rend="italic">and</hi> police’ but ‘towards the p.’—The reading in lq seems to me an interpolation, made when ‘have’, having become more of an auxiliary, more rarely meant ‘possess’. The same meaning ‘to enjoy peace (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1e)’ also II Atr 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_5.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= ‘werdet’, wie Schmid übersetzt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= ‘become’, as Schmid translates</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIEm_5.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 1, 1–4; 20, 3.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIEm_5.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Or perhaps ‘suppression of fighting’ as compared with the suppression of thefts.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIEm_5.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">10</biblScope></bibl><label>fylston</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wel f.</hi> H.</seg></note>
